{"kind":"report","text":"Independent review of exact 888bb29dd7a0f62484e364029f812d3e01873eb1, primary 242b3364, implementation 55563589: changes requested. Revision 2 correctly records Hugh's D1/D5/D6 decisions and adds useful measurement and write-storm work, but its 45-line addition/3-line deletion does not repair the six findings in prior verdict git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c935a4b96d7f7d9509a6a4aa03b18ffa98ed5cc6. Those findings are restated below so this verdict is self-contained. Repair the report and affected durable handoffs on the same audit request/promise; all follow-ups need not be implemented before the audit can land.\n\nArchitecture: This head changes only the audit note; its production tree is byte-identical to a6330262. Room admission/authority, independently verified log bytes, Git-owned remote-effect ledgers, runner isolation and operator interfaces are the affected boundaries. The proposed simplification must preserve those contracts. No new runtime guard is added, so mutation testing is not owed for this documentation head.\n\nSecurity: The two invitation defects warrant prompt repair under c657d4ba. Several other claims currently blur demonstrated defects, intentional trust models and investigation. Correct those distinctions below; keep public founding and checker-attestation choices with their recorded owner decisions.\n\nSimplification: Consolidation is worthwhile where behavior is shared. Blanket table deletion, global uniqueness of exported type names and unsupported deployment knobs do not make the platform clearer. Keep the complete functional scope; sequencing/estimates do not waive functionality.\n\n1. [P1] Protect ownership and the complete verification prefix in the retention handoff (note COST-14, lines261-262; request 99782949). That request explicitly includes entries and duty tables in a retention sweep for closed rows, and its acceptance test only asks that old closed rows disappear. Closed does not mean disposable. packages/git/src/workspace/workspaces.ts:776-793 reads a done repo-create row with done_reason='sealed' to recover the sealed incarnation and exclude it from abandoned-name cleanup. Deleting it loses ownership provenance. docs/protocol.md R-LOG-1/2/7/10 also requires the complete signed prefix, retained replay inputs and earlier publication commitments. Amend the durable request to retain referenced closed ownership rows, entries and retained verification data, or specify an equivalent durable archive with compatible readers and restart/replay tests. Unknown mint/create effects remain owned until resolved; a deadline or sweep cannot discard them. State which tables/queries are actually missing indexes; landing/core.ts:106 already has a state/ord index. Partial indexes and backoff remain useful. The new section10 FIFO cap on idem compounds this finding: docs/protocol.md:510-527 R-IDEM-2/3 requires the original result or mismatch without re-admission, and R-IDEM-5 explicitly requires records to last as long as the room. Deleting older keys lets a still-valid signed act be admitted again or erases its mismatch protection; an archive must preserve exact lookup, original results and lifetime uniqueness. Bound attention without dropping unresolved work or breaking its monotonic cursor/read contract; preserve equivalent durable readers where data moves. Do not import woo's FIFO policy as if it were compatible with Artroom's lifetime replay contract. Keep unknown remote effects owned. Correct both the note and the authoritative handoff before implementation.\n\n2. [P1] Replace unsupported container acceptance criteria (COST-03/13; requests d2cb872f and 2b1d287e). packages/room/wrangler.jsonc uses scheduling_policy='durable_object'; publisher/container.ts:152 selects the image at ctx.container.start, and checkers/src/sandbox.ts:134 already selects instance='standard-1'. Cloudflare's current primary documentation says this policy does not support max_instances, and its size is the runtime instance property, defaulting to lite. Demanding Wrangler instance_type/max_instances is not implementable for this deployment. Amend the report and requests to use supported runtime sizing and durable application admission/concurrency/budget controls. Preserve the current scheduling policy unless a separately justified migration is intended; changing it is not a routine quota fix. Sources: https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/configuration/scheduling-policy/ and https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/api/durable-object-container/ (checked 2026-10-02).\n\n3. [P2] Correct the byte contract and credit existing tests before centralising signing (summary52-54, DUP-01:273-280; request 4cd9b14f). log/src/crypto.ts:94-95 signs entry-v1 over raw UTF-8 hash bytes, not always canonical JSON, exactly as room/src/crypto.ts:143-150 does. Canonicalising that hash string would add JSON quotes and invalidate historical signatures. room/test/workerd/log.test.ts:49-83 already publishes Room-produced entries, verifies both publications with the independent log verifier and rejects tampering. The missing coverage is comprehensive cross-implementation edge vectors, not 'nothing tests' compatibility. Amend the note and handoff to preserve domain-dependent bytes, historical hashes/signatures, synchronous Room sealing and runtime/dependency boundaries; add missing vectors before switching implementations. Preserve deliberate input-layer differences through explicit adapters, rather than silently changing admitted inputs.\n\n4. [P2] Make the security evidence and assurances precise (ranked rows3/10, SEC-04/07/10/12 and checked-and-sound). A placeholder URL establishes a misconfiguration risk, not that a third party owns the host or token theft has occurred. SEC-10's verifier checks the caller-selected remote and reports room/operator identity (log/src/verify.ts:119-125,150-155; cli.ts:28-36; R-LOG-10). Missing optional identity/checkpoint pinning is useful hardening; identify a concrete consumer that confuses an unexpected room with an expected room before ranking it as a demonstrated integrity attack. SEC-12 provides no key class, registration path or code citation: distinguish registration lockout from signature forgery, and label backend-specific work as investigation. log/src/crypto.ts:108-114 and Room's Noble fallback:188 use zip215:false; pinned Noble 2.4.0 rejects small-order public keys in that mode. The WebCrypto path needs separate conformance evidence. Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paulmillr/noble-curves/2.4.0/src/abstract/edwards.ts . Finally, sandbox.ts:75-80,134-139 permits registry GET/HEAD through its gateway: say unrestricted internet is disabled, with explicit permitted egress, rather than 'no internet'. requests.ts:189 validates the outer redemption before its limiter; distinguish that from the later validation of the client join body. Keep the actual invitation and body-boundary defects.\n\n5. [P2] Make the cost estimates reproducible and the deployment requirements consistent (ranked78, profiles205-206, COST-02/06/09/10, section8/requests table). Link the actual pricing/limit pages, show counts multiplied by rates with account-wide included allocations distinguished from marginal room cost, and state the per-attempt provider operations for each failed-work path. A five-second alarm count alone does not establish a $155-777 bill: the apparent arithmetic assumes 2-10 billed Artifacts operations on each of 518,400 attempts, which must be justified by source paths and the explicitly uncertain token-operation billing. Include runner instance/CPU-time and DO duration assumptions for the active profile. The lite account capacity also meets the 30 TB disk limit at roughly 15,000 two-GB instances before 24,000 reaches 1,500 vCPU; do not present CPU as the first limit. Founding uses first-commit.ts's direct smart-HTTP push; Publisher startup follows repository work/publication rather than necessarily allocating a container inside each founding call. Every landing refreshes current previews, but core.ts:1303-1304 and jobs.ts:102-118 issue only clean/unlanded, unmet, bound and deduplicated obligations, not universally every check. Orphan pending cohorts can follow the5-second pending wake, not universally 60 seconds. Room.tick and jobTokenDuties already exist as DO RPCs (room.ts:173-184), and Wrangler observability is enabled; distinguish missing documented operator routes/application telemetry from absence of any logs/RPCs. Section8 says everything else follows the jam, while d2cb872f's table says before J2; resolve that sequencing contradiction. Sources: https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/platform/pricing/ , https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/platform/pricing/ , https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/platform/limits/ , https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/pricing/ .\n\n6. [P2] Reconcile current-base evidence and narrow structural acceptance (LAYER-01:371-373; requests 894c9030 and 4fd06c76). Git lacks a unified migration runner, but snapshot/repos.ts:148-152 already has transactional schema-version2 adoption/upgrade (also present at 93a2552e). At this candidate jobs.ts:39,217-219 already imports completeInventory exported by git/index.ts:54. Credit those repairs and preserve their in-flight legacy ownership semantics instead of requesting a second implementation. The condition 'no two exported types share a name across packages' in 4fd06c76 would also prohibit deliberate shared type reexports (room/ports.ts:53 etc) and harmless package namespaces. Scope it to the cited distinct/confusing contracts and intentional import aliases/shared definitions. Finally, the note says every finding was reopened by planner while its Reported definition says it was not (15-20); use an honest, consistent confidence definition and add missing file/line evidence for Reported findings, including SEC-12/13, COST-05/08/13/14, DUP-05-11 and cited but undefined ARCH/LAYER IDs. Request 55563589 explicitly requires reproducible evidence for every finding.\n\n7. [P2] Correct the new Verified write-storm mapping (section10:445-479; assert53fbb7e3 and request8bd623cc). admission.ts:266-273 checks idem first; the two INSERTs:1493/1510 apply to newly recorded acceptance/refusal, not identical retries or every act. Classify this as lifetime growth of unique recorded requests, not a demonstrated retry-mints-a-row loop. store.ts:97-110 checks schema_version and skips completed steps; RoomCore construction invokes createSchema, but a current store does not replay all eight migrations on each object wake. Distinguish genuinely fresh storage initialization from reconstruction of an existing DO and measure both. Six explicit secondary indexes are spread over the Room's tables, with additional implicit uniqueness indexes; they are not six writes on each entry or a uniform multiplier per act. Attribute rows to the actual tables/indexes each path changes, including alarm writes and deletes. Policy/landing fanout likewise needs the qualifying/dedup conditions in finding5. Woo's scripts at6d2c425a correctly motivate provider measurement; their implementation is reference material, not evidence that Artroom has already met a billing gate. Count deletes/pruning in budgets too: Cloudflare bills each setAlarm as one written row and counts deletes as rows written (https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/pricing/, reopened2026-10-02). Preserve read-only analytics credentials and spike-only measurement constraints of8bd623cc. Resolve the new 'before J2' requirement against section8's 'everything else can follow the jam'.\n\nValidation: exact clean clone /tmp/artroom-checker-simplification-v2 at888bb29d; read the full prior465-line note and the complete revision2 delta plus changed sections, inspected the current invitation/primary and implementation chain, all original fifteen handoffs, the owner decisions and new53fbb7e3/8bd623cc/73eccbec records. Reopened the lifetime-idempotency contract, admission inserts/replay lookup, migration version guard and woo's billing-query script; rechecked current Cloudflare primary pricing/scheduling docs. git diff --check passes. The production tree remains byte-identical to a6330262; only the507-line audit note differs. Prior independent security/cost/architecture cross-checks still apply to unchanged claims. No new runtime guard, source mutation, provider operation or fresh runtime-suite claim.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:242b3364ddbc2b9c76d42d2734e6b0ee6252d2fc","binding":"assigned","head":"888bb29dd7a0f62484e364029f812d3e01873eb1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:98a80939f98dddb6cc0fb764feacb3156381402f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a3426987d087f1ce394d8a2072fedf5e425d1d0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3445eae059394ed3143293792021480272a644a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}